opi — how to do things
Installed by pi-bootstrap (file home-README in that repo); edits here are replaced on the next run.
Details: ~/claude/docker/README.md, ~/claude/docker/RESTORE.md, ~/claude/pi-bootstrap/README.md

SSH
  into the router (from this Pi)          ssh router
  into this Pi (from another device)      ssh -i ~/.ssh/opi_ed25519 pi@192.168.1.11
                                          (keys only, no passwords; the key + how-to: GitHub repo ssh-keys)
  get my SSH keys on a new device         gh repo clone prithivirajasingh5/ssh-keys && cd ssh-keys && git-crypt unlock

WireGuard (VPN into home from outside)
  phone: show a peer's QR code to scan    docker exec wireguard /app/show-peer prip
                                          (peers: prip pril nithp nithl others1 others2 others3 others4)
  laptop: import this config file         ~/claude/docker/wireguard/config/peer_prip/peer_prip.conf
  server address                          opi.prithivirajasingh.com:51820 (UDP)
  who is connected                        docker exec wireguard wg show

Files and media
  shares, Windows                         \\192.168.1.11\Movies   \\192.168.1.11\Archives   \\192.168.1.11\samba_share
  shares, macOS / Linux / phone           smb://192.168.1.11/Movies
  qBittorrent web                         http://192.168.1.11:8080
  torrent watcher: what it did            docker logs --tail 30 torrentwatch

Docker stack
  status of all containers                cd ~/claude/docker && docker compose ps
  logs of one container                   docker logs --tail 30 <container>
  apply a change to one service           cd ~/claude/docker && docker compose up -d <service>
  run the tests                           ~/claude/docker/python-jobs/run-tests

Router and network
  router web page                         http://192.168.1.1
  put our router scripts back             bash ~/claude/docker/router/install.sh --enable
  network watch summary                   cat ~/claude/docker/shared/netwatch/summary.txt
  network watch alerts                    tail ~/claude/docker/shared/netwatch/alerts.jsonl

Telegram bot
  list its commands                       send "ls" to the bot
  devices on the network / block one      send "router ls" / "router tv block 30m"
  tell me when a device comes / goes      send "router bathroom-light notify" (stop: "... notify off")
  send a message from this Pi             messenger "text"

Claude Code
  use it                                  Claude app -> Code -> opi
  is it running                           systemctl status claude-remote
  renew sign-in                           send "claude login" to the Telegram bot, then "claude <code>"
  update it now                           /usr/local/bin/claude-weekly-update

Health and setup
  health facts now                        AI=0 SEND=0 health-report
  full health report to Telegram          sudo systemctl start health-report
  re-run the Pi setup (safe to repeat)    bash ~/claude/pi-bootstrap/bootstrap.sh
